From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:25:20 +0800
Subject: wifi: ath11k: replace a pairwise key in place

mac80211 replaces an in-use PTK by calling set_key() with DISABLE_KEY
for the old key and SET_KEY for the new one, which ath11k sends to the
firmware as an install of cipher NONE followed by an install of the
new key. This is the clear-then-install sequence that commit
97acb0259cc9 ("wifi: ath11k: fix group data packet drops during
rekey") stopped for group keys, and it fails the same way for a
pairwise key: on an IPQ8074 AP, the station stopped receiving at its
first PTK rekey in 6 of 6 runs, with a Broadcom and a Qualcomm client,
the REO counted up to 165 PN check failures per run, and hostapd
deauthenticated the station at the next rekey. Because ath11k does not
set NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CAN_REPLACE_PTK0, mac80211 also warns "Rekeying
PTK for STA ... but driver can't safely do that" and flushes the
queues, which waits ATH11K_FLUSH_TIMEOUT (5 s) for the whole radio
whenever a busy station keeps frames pending.

Keep the old pairwise key in the firmware when mac80211 disables it for
a station, so that the following SET_KEY overwrites it in place, as the
group key path already does. Outside raw mode the hardware encrypts a
frame with the key it holds for the peer and generates the PN, so a
frame queued across the replace leaves with the old key or the new one
and never in the clear, and the SET_KEY resets the REO PN state. A
pairwise key removed without a replacement is cleared when the station
leaves the authorized state, and peer deletion drops it with the peer.
With this, advertise NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CAN_REPLACE_PTK0.

With hostapd rekeying the PTK every 20 s, a download to a FastConnect
7800 station holds 914 to 945 Mbit/s through four rekeys, with no
second below 854 Mbit/s (3 runs); before, the station lost the
connection in 3 of 3 runs.

Closes: https://github.com/JuliusBairaktaris/openwrt-ppe-nss/issues/58

Limit deferred clearing to authorized peers using hardware encryption.
Keep raw removal unchanged and preserve PN type while the old key is
still installed, including unrelated GTK deletion. Clear a deferred slot before installing a different key
index, and retain its pending state until both WMI and REO clearing succeed.
Return clearing errors during deauthorization; NSS revocation is kept by
the subsequent integration group before the deferred key is cleared.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
@@ -576,6 +576,14 @@
 
 	bool use_4addr_set;
